VERIFIED    DV33-11 [Onkelos Deut 33:28; Onkelos Deut 33:29; Sifrei Devarim 356:4; Sifrei Devarim 356:5; Sifrei Devarim 356:6; Sifrei Devarim 356:7; Sifrei Devarim 356:8; Sifrei Devarim 356:9; Sifrei Devarim 356:10; Sifrei Devarim 356:11; Sifrei Devarim 356:12; Sifrei Devarim 356:13; Sifrei Devarim 356:14] AND ISRAEL DWELLS IN SAFETY, THE FOUNTAIN OF JACOB ALONE, IN A LAND OF CORN AND WINE, YEA, HIS HEAVENS DROP DOWN DEW; HAPPY ARE YOU, O ISRAEL, WHO IS LIKE YOU, A PEOPLE SAVED BY THE LORD, THE SHIELD OF YOUR HELP AND THE SWORD OF YOUR EXCELLENCY; AND YOUR ENEMIES SHALL DWINDLE AWAY BEFORE YOU, AND YOU SHALL TREAD UPON THEIR HIGH PLACES. The Sifrei (piska 356:4-14, eleven rows): safety is security — Onkelos's word again (356:4); 'alone' Balaam's word, not Moses' 32:12 nor Jeremiah's (356:5); the fountain Jacob's blessing of Genesis 48:21, the corn Isaac's of 27:28, the dew Isaiah's (356:6-8); 'who is like you' answered by the Holy Spirit and the tutor's garden — happy are you, what is prepared for you (356:9); salvation by the Shekhinah alone (356:10); the shield of 2 Samuel 22:3 (356:11); the sword the ornaments of Horeb sworn back (356:12); the enemies' feigned brotherhood — Esau and Hiram (356:13); THE NECKS OF THE KINGS at Makkedah, Joshua 10:24 — the spine's last row on the chapter (356:14). Onkelos: 'as the blessing with which Jacob their father blessed them' for the fountain (33:28); 'happy are you, Israel, there is none like you', the redemption from before the LORD, 'strong in your help', the victories of your might, the high places 'THE NECKS OF THEIR KINGS' — one teaching with the Sifrei's last row (33:29). The ink: 'the fountain of Jacob', 'drop down dew', 'happy are you, O Israel', 'a people saved by the LORD', 'the shield of your help', 'the sword of your excellency', 'tread upon their high places' once in the Bible; 'who is like you' the one phrase with psalm seats beside it; the Name with bet once in the chapter (33:29); 33:28 with 2 Kings 18:32 and Isaiah 36:17 (four in order, cited); Isaac's 'corn and wine' spelled defective, Moses' full; 33:28 and 32:2 (the dew), 33:29 and 32:13 (the high places, two spellings) twins by sense with no shared token; Genesis 15:1's shield the Torah kin.
